Package: qnca
Type: Package
Title: Quantile Necessary Condition Analysis
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R: person("Marek", "Deja", email = "marek.deja@uj.edu.pl",
    role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-0015-2322"))
Description: Estimates quantile necessity frontiers for Necessary Condition
    Analysis (NCA) of Dul (2016) <doi:10.1177/1094428115584005>. For a
    tolerance pi in (0, 1], the frontier at each outcome target is a low
    type-1 quantile of the condition among the cases that attain the target,
    and 1 - pi is the share of those cases allowed below the reported
    requirement. The package reports the empty-zone effect size with its
    permutation p-value, bottleneck tables, a target-by-target account of the
    frontier, deletion and addition screens, a proposed dependence-matched
    reference band and a consistency probe. At pi = 1 the frontier is the
    ceiling envelopment-free disposal hull (CE-FDH) ceiling of NCA, which the
    package checks against its own CE-FDH implementation and against the
    'NCA' package.
